!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: HeLa cell
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: CAS9#W7
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: control
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = The sgRNA-expressing cells were treated with 50 pg/ml STx1 twice in two weeks.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = HeLa CAS9#W7 cells were maintained in Dulbecco’s modified Eagle’s medium (DMEM) containing 10% fetal bovine serum (FBS) with 7.5μg/ml blasticidin . HeLa CAS9#W7 cells were infected with the pooled lentiviruses to express sgRNAs.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA from the frozen cells was purified by the conventional phenol-chloroform method.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = First PCR amplification was carried out with 20 cycles using PrimeStar GXL DNA polymerase (Takara, Otsu, Japan) and the following primers (9 forward primers and 1 reverse primer): (Fw) 1stY1R1s0-8: CTACACGACGCTCTTCCGATCT[-/N/NN/NNN/NNNN/NNNNN/NNNNNN/NNNNNNN/NNNNNNNN]TCTTGTGGAAAGGACGAAACACCG (included 0-8 bp random sequence for increasing library complexity); and (Rv) 1stY2as: GCCACTTTTTCAAGTTGATAACGGACTAG. Second PCR amplification was carried out with 10 cycles using the following primers: (Fw) 2nd P5R1s:  AATGATACGGCGACCACCGAGATCTACACTCTTTCCCTACACGACGCTCTTCCGATCT; and (Rv) 2nd P7Y2as: CAAGCAGAAGACGGCATACGAGAT[CC/TT/AA/GG]GCCACTTTTTCAAGTTGATAACGGACTAG (included barcodes for multiplexing of different samples).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Amplicon sequencing of sgRNA in GeCKO v2.0 library plasmid
!Sample_description = GeCKO v2 library A, biological replicate 1, control, amplicon sequencing of sgRNA region in GeCKO v2.0 library plasmid
!Sample_description = STx_GeCKOv2_LibA_mageck.sgrna_summary.txt
!Sample_description = STx_GeCKOv2_LibA_mageck.gene_summary.txt
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina RTA1.18.54 software used for basecalling
!Sample_data_processing = 5' and 3' adapter and low quality trimming using skewer program (version 0.1.126)
!Sample_data_processing = Quality filtering (at Phred >= Q20) with split_libraries_fastq.py (version 1.9.1) of QIIME program
!Sample_data_processing = Read count of sgRNA using "sort" and "uniq" of unix command program
!Sample_data_processing = Reads align to sgRNA of Human GeCKO v2 library A/B
!Sample_data_processing = Normalization with following formula; normalized reads per sgRNA = reads per sgRNA / total reads for all sgRNAs in sample x 10^7
!Sample_data_processing = Statistic analysis using MAGeCK program (version 0.5.7)
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: Human GeCKO v2 library A/B
